Z||000000||TRiAD||06-10-2001||06:22 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.lamborghiniregistry.com/Events/ItalianHappening1999/Ital-2.gif">  <P>The red Lamborghini Islero in this pic! (ser#6096). <P>I met this guy by way of his webpage  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/LuigiDVM/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/LuigiDVM/</A> <BR>and found out he was only 1/2 hr away form me! The Islero is my favorite "GT" car, and my favorite F/R Lamborghini, following only the Countach as my favorite car of all time. <BR>It has a DOHC 48V 4.0L V12 with 6 dual-barrel webbers, and a 5sp manual. It's a 2+2 (2 door coupe with smallish rear seats), and is a BALL to drive!<P>It drives very solidly, and has an exhaust note to die for!<P>~Thought I'd share.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">  <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 06-10-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cheever2||06-10-2001||06:33 PM||||You'll never get a job at a magazine or TV show, with a review like that.  Come on, take us through the experience.  You're our eyes and ears, give us every little feeling of every little turn & bump.  Was the ride hard or soft?  Does the car lean in turns or not?  Is the back end skittish, or does it go just where you point it?  How do the steering wheel and shifter knob feel in your hands?  How's the headroom, legroom?  Etc etc etc.<P>I'm happy for your experience, but don't tease us.  That's just cruel.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||TRiAD||06-10-2001||08:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>You'll never get a job at a magazine or TV show, with a review like that.  Come on, take us through the experience.  You're our eyes and ears, give us every little feeling of every little turn & bump.  Was the ride hard or soft?  Does the car lean in turns or not?  Is the back end skittish, or does it go just where you point it?  How do the steering wheel and shifter knob feel in your hands?  How's the headroom, legroom?  Etc etc etc.<P>I'm happy for your experience, but don't tease us.  That's just cruel.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's funny you say that, being an automotive journalist is one of my lifeling dreams! As it is, I'm working on an article telling about the day for his newsletter. I will post it here first, as soon as it's done. <BR>You will want one once you read it!<BR>I know I'll be saving my nickels.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
